      "results": [
        {
          "ruleId": "hdr-csp",
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "Content-Security-Policy header missing\n\nEvidence: Header not present\n\nExplanation: Without a CSP, browsers cannot restrict which scripts, styles, or resources the page may load, making XSS attacks more impactful.\n\nFix: Add a Content-Security-Policy header. Start with Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self' and progressively tighten it."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "http://127.0.0.1:59205/"
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "severity": "medium",
            "checkId": "hdr-csp"
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "hdr-xfo",
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "X-Frame-Options or CSP frame-ancestors missing\n\nEvidence: X-Frame-Options: absent; CSP frame-ancestors: absent\n\nExplanation: Without framing protection, this page can be embedded in an attacker-controlled iframe, enabling clickjacking attacks.\n\nFix: Add X-Frame-Options: DENY (or SAMEORIGIN), or add frame-ancestors 'self' to your Content-Security-Policy."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "http://127.0.0.1:59205/"
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "severity": "low",
            "checkId": "hdr-xfo"
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "hdr-xcto",
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff missing\n\nEvidence: Header not present\n\nExplanation: Without nosniff, some browsers may MIME-sniff responses and execute content as a different type than declared (e.g., execute a JSONP endpoint as a script).\n\nFix: Add: X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff"
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "http://127.0.0.1:59205/"
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "severity": "low",
            "checkId": "hdr-xcto"
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "hdr-referrer",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Referrer-Policy header missing\n\nEvidence: Header not present\n\nExplanation: Without Referrer-Policy, the browser's default behaviour may leak full URLs (including query parameters with sensitive data) to third-party sites via the Referer header.\n\nFix: Add: Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin"
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "http://127.0.0.1:59205/"
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "severity": "info",
            "checkId": "hdr-referrer"
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "hdr-permissions",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Permissions-Policy header missing\n\nEvidence: Header not present\n\nExplanation: Without Permissions-Policy (formerly Feature-Policy), powerful browser features (camera, microphone, geolocation) may be accessible to embedded third-party iframes.\n\nFix: Add a Permissions-Policy header to restrict which browser features this page and its embedded content may use."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "http://127.0.0.1:59205/"
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "severity": "info",
            "checkId": "hdr-permissions"
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "cookie-flags",
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "Cookie 'session_id' missing HttpOnly flag\n\nEvidence: Set-Cookie: session_id=... (HttpOnly absent)\n\nExplanation: The cookie 'session_id' is accessible to JavaScript. If the site has an XSS vulnerability, an attacker can steal this cookie.\n\nFix: Add the HttpOnly flag: Set-Cookie: name=value; HttpOnly; ..."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "http://127.0.0.1:59205/"
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "severity": "medium",
            "checkId": "cookie-flags"
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "redirect-https",
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "Site is served over plain HTTP\n\nEvidence: Target URL uses scheme: http\n\nExplanation: The site is not using HTTPS. All traffic including credentials and session tokens is transmitted in plaintext and can be intercepted by anyone on the network path.\n\nFix: Obtain a TLS certificate and configure the server to serve all content over HTTPS. Redirect all HTTP traffic to HTTPS."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "http://127.0.0.1:59205"
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "severity": "medium",
            "checkId": "redirect-https"
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "exposed-files",
          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": ".git/HEAD exposed\n\nEvidence: HTTP 200, size=21 bytes, body starts with 'ref: refs/heads/main\\n'\n\nExplanation: Git repository HEAD file is publicly accessible\n\nFix: Remove or restrict access to /.git/HEAD. Ensure your web server does not serve sensitive files. Add these paths to your .gitignore and review deployment scripts."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "http://127.0.0.1:59205/.git/HEAD"
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "severity": "high",
            "checkId": "exposed-files"
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "exposed-files",
          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": ".env file exposed\n\nEvidence: HTTP 200, size=37 bytes\n\nExplanation: .env environment file is publicly accessible\n\nFix: Remove or restrict access to /.env. Ensure your web server does not serve sensitive files. Add these paths to your .gitignore and review deployment scripts."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "http://127.0.0.1:59205/.env"
                }
              }
